        <mxCell id="0la0HrTPfz4GJbjPKGwh-35" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;1. Allocate new data buffer (make_dat creates a new pyop2 Dat that now reads the updated node_set)&lt;div&gt;2. Migrate values from old buffer to new buffer via SF bcast (input ordering SF maps each particle in new VOM to its particle id in the old VOM using (input rank, input index) pairs&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="210" x="1270" y="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
